  "executive_summary": "The Docker environment hosting the ICS lab presents multiple high-risk attack paths to the physical process. The most critical vulnerabilities are the simulation container's unrestricted Docker socket access (E8) and the router container's multi-network bridging with elevated capabilities (E7). These create direct pathways for container escape and network manipulation. The PLC and EWS containers (E2, E3) have CAP_NET_ADMIN and root execution, which could allow protocol-level attacks if compromised. The HMI and kali containers (E4, E6) also have network capabilities that could be exploited via the DMZ network. All containers on the ICS network (plc, EWS, simulation) have no resource limits or hardened security profiles, weakening isolation. The audit agent container (E1) has no direct process network access but could be used for lateral movement if other vectors are exploited.",
